          <a href="#setup" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Placement and Starting</a>
          <a href="#skip" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. Who Should Buy Another Size</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. FAQ</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. Common Mistakes</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          A 6,500 watt generator is two different machines: a 5,000 watt-class generator with a 6,500 watt surge rating, or a true 6,500 running-watt generator that nearly fills a 30-amp transfer switch. For a house with a well pump, buy the second kind. For a fridge, freezer, furnace and lights, either works, and the first kind can be an inverter.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="two-meanings" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. The Two Kinds of 6500 Watt Generator
          </h2>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Peak Rating vs Running Rating</h3>

          <p>
            "6500 watt generator" means two different machines, and the difference is about 1,500 watts. Most generators sold as 6,500 watts quote that number as starting or peak watts, the short burst available for a second or two while a motor spins up. Their running output, the number you can actually load them to for hours, is usually 5,000 to 5,500 watts. The Briggs & Stratton Q6500 is the classic example: 6,500 starting, 5,000 running. A smaller group quotes 6,500 as running watts, with starting watts around 8,000. The Generac GP6500 and Champion 201169 are both 6,500 running and 8,125 starting.
          </p>

          <p>
            Both are legitimate, but they are different sizes of generator. The first group is a 5,000 watt-class machine with a generous surge rating. The second is close to the top of what a 30-amp transfer switch can carry. The price, weight and fuel burn of each follow from the running number, not the label. When you compare listings, cross out the big number on the box and look for the words rated or running.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Model</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Running watts (gas)</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Starting watts (gas)</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">240V twist-lock</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Type</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Generac GP6500 7683</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">6,500</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">8,125</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">L14-30R, 27.1A</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Open frame</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Champion 201169</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">6,500</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">8,125</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">L14-30R, 27A</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Open frame, tri fuel</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Honda EU7000iS</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">5,500</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">7,000</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">L14-30R, 22.9A</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Inverter</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">WEN DF680iX</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">5,100</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">6,800</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">L14-30R, 21.25A</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Inverter, dual fuel</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Briggs & Stratton Q6500</td>
