            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Will a 6500 watt generator run a well pump?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Usually, if it has around 8,000 starting watts. A one-horsepower submersible pump can need 4,000 watts or more to start, on top of whatever else is running. The Generac GP6500 and Champion 201169, both rated 8,125 starting watts, handle that. Models with 6,500 starting watts may need the fridge and freezer switched off while the pump starts.
              </p>
