            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a 6500 watt inverter generator worth it?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                If quiet matters, yes. Inverters like the WEN DF680iX, Briggs Q6500 and Honda EU7000iS are much quieter than open frames and burn less fuel at light loads. But at this size they give 5,000 to 5,500 running watts rather than 6,500, so for a well pump or a long load list an open-frame model delivers more power for the money.
              </p>
