          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most houses, the Generac GP6500 is the 6500 watt generator to buy: it actually runs 6,500 watts, starts a well pump on top of the essentials, and nearly fills a 30-amp transfer switch, at an open-frame price. If you have natural gas or prefer propane, the Champion 201169 gives similar power on every fuel. If quiet matters more than headroom, the WEN DF680iX is the value inverter and the Honda EU7000iS the premium one.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, read past the number on the box. Running watts on your fuel, the 240 volt amperage and the starting watts of your largest motor decide whether a 6,500 watt generator runs your house, and they differ by more than 1,500 watts between generators that carry the same label.
